Here's how to implement all three requirements:

## 1. Custom "Cancel" Back Button (on EditProductPage)

```xml
<!-- EditProductPage.xaml -->
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.Views.EditProductPage">

    <Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
        <BackButtonBehavior TextOverride="Cancel"
                           Command="{Binding BackCommand}" />
    </Shell.BackButtonBehavior>

    <!-- your form content -->
</ContentPage>
```

The `BackCommand` in your ViewModel handles the custom back tap:

```csharp
[RelayCommand]
async Task Back()
{
    if (HasUnsavedChanges)
    {
        bool discard = await Shell.Current.DisplayAlert(
            "Unsaved Changes",
            "Discard your changes?",
            "Discard", "Stay");
        if (!discard) return;
    }
    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
}
```

## 2. Guard the System Back Gesture / Hardware Button

The `BackButtonBehavior.Command` only handles the **toolbar** back button. For the Android hardware/gesture back and any other `Pop` navigation, add a guard in `AppShell.xaml.cs`:

```csharp
// AppShell.xaml.cs
protected override async void OnNavigating(ShellNavigatingEventArgs args)
{
    base.OnNavigating(args);

    // Only intercept backward (Pop) navigation
    if (args.Source != ShellNavigationSource.Pop)
        return;

    // Check if the current page is EditProductPage
    if (Shell.Current.CurrentPage is EditProductPage page
        && page.BindingContext is EditProductViewModel vm
        && vm.HasUnsavedChanges)
    {
        var deferral = args.GetDeferral();   // required for async work
        bool discard = await Shell.Current.DisplayAlert(
            "Unsaved Changes",
            "Discard your changes?",
            "Discard", "Stay");
        if (!discard)
            args.Cancel();       // user chose "Stay" — cancel navigation
        deferral.Complete();     // always complete the deferral
    }
}
```

### Key points

| Concern | Mechanism |
|---|---|
| Custom "Cancel" text | `BackButtonBehavior.TextOverride` |
| Toolbar back tap | `BackButtonBehavior.Command` → ViewModel |
| System/gesture back | `OnNavigating` + `GetDeferral()` in AppShell |
| Cancel navigation | `args.Cancel()` before `deferral.Complete()` |

> **Pitfall:** You must call `GetDeferral()` before any `await`. Without it, the navigation completes before your async dialog finishes, and `args.Cancel()` has no effect.
